<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Caucasus</p><h1 class="st-title">Sajid Emirate</h1><p class="st-meta">889 CE – 929 CE · capital Ardabil</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">An Abbasid governorship turned hereditary emirate in Azerbaijan whose emir Yusuf dominated Armenia and executed its king Smbat I.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sajid-dynasty">Sajids</a> were descended from a military family from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/usrushana">Ushrusana</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a>, in the service of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphs</a>. In 889 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-ibn-abil-saj">Muhammad ibn Abi'l-Saj</a> was appointed governor of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a> and ruled it almost independently from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maragha">Maragha</a> and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ardabil">Ardabil</a>, founding a hereditary <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a> under the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir">emirs</a> controlled north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> and claimed authority over <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/armenia">Armenia</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/albania">Albania</a> as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid</a> governors, collecting tribute and backing rival Armenian princes. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yusuf-ibn-abil-saj">Yusuf ibn Abi'l-Saj</a> invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a>, captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/smbat-i-of-armenia">Smbat I of Bagratid Armenia</a> and had him executed in 914, while crowning <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gagik-i-of-vaspurakan">Gagik Artsruni</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-vaspurakan">Kingdom of Vaspurakan</a> as a rival king.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Yusuf was killed in 928 fighting the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qarmatians">Qarmatians</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a> collapsed in 929 amid struggles among his commanders. The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sallarid-emirate">Sallarid Emirate</a> and other local dynasties took over <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/sajid-emirate.jpg" alt="Sajid Emirate" width="320" height="221"><figcaption>Image: Arab_Hafez, edited by HistoryofIran (me). · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SajidDynastyMapHistoryofIran.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>889 CE – 929 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Ardabil</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Muhammad ibn Abi'l-Saj, Yusuf ibn Abi'l-Saj</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic; Persian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/iran">Iran</a>, <a href="/countries/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a>, <a href="/countries/armenia">Armenia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Sajids, Sajid dynasty</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=909&amp;focus=sajid-emirate" aria-label="Sajid Emirate on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5836 832 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Sajid Emirate lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6156 1088L6079 1051M6156 1088L6134 1224M6156 1088L6202 1060"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6079 1051h0M6134 1224h0M6202 1060h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6156 1088h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6156 1088h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its capital. <a href="/atlas?y